title: Potential Citrix NetScaler Memory Overflow Exploitation (CVE-2026-8452)
id: b4d8e1a3-6f2c-4b7a-9e5d-1c3a8f0b2d4e
status: experimental
description: Detects potential exploitation attempts against Citrix NetScaler ADC/Gateway appliances via CVE-2026-8452 memory overflow. Monitor for anomalous Gateway VPN/AAA virtual server activity and unexpected root shell spawning on NetScaler appliances.
references:
  - https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/cisa-orders-patch-citrix-netscaler-rce
  - https://www.securityweek.com/citrix-netscaler-rce-cve-2026-8452
  - https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026-08-28
tags:
  - attack.t1190
logsource:
  category: process_creation
  product: netscaler
detection:
  selection_gateway:
    EventID: 300010
    Description|contains:
      - 'Gateway'
      - 'AAA'
  selection_shell_spawn:
    EventID: 1
    Image|endswith:
      - '/bin/sh'
      - '/bin/bash'
    ParentImage|contains:
      - 'nscmond'
      - 'nsaadclientd'
      - 'nsppe'
  condition: selection_gateway and selection_shell_spawn
falsepositives:
  - Authorized administrative access to NetScaler appliances
  - Legitimate Gateway VPN session handling
level: critical
